# Continual-ARC task-679ab180 notes

Instance over at attempt cap; avoid repeating speculative hypotheses. Grid background 3, marker color 6 bars: top row cols 13-16 (0-indexed); bottom row cols 6-9. Single color-1 cells at (r,c)=(5,7),(18,9),(20,8). Demos establish a generic rule: edge marker bars indicate lines/areas to draw from their color-coded boundary; isolated points determine extents, and the output commonly draws rays/stripes in the point's own color, with color 4 marking terminal point/next-to-marker cells. Exact rule remains uncertain due to failure to compare all demos. Available demos: 
1) 8x27 bg1, top/bottom 7 triplets; 0 points at (2,13),(5,14): output creates right-edge vertical 0-filled strip columns 25-26, and writes 4 at (2,13),(5,14) while other 0 marks retained; 
2) 12x11 bg7, 2x2 color2 endpoints top-left and bottom-right; color8 points (2,7),(6,6), output fills first two columns with 8 between endpoints; point rays/marker terminals 4; 
3) 24x26 bg7 with top bar color8 c6-10 and bottom bar c0-4, points color1 (8,8),(13,9),(17,10); output fills columns 2-4 with color1 from top to bottom and right-side bands/lines per point with 4 marking boundary; 
4) 18x21 bg2, color1 bars at left rows9-10 and right rows16-17, color0 point (10,10); output extends horizontal row10 from left through point, zeros and 4 terminal at c10, and extends bottom boundary row17 to left;
5) 21x6 bg3, color9 bars left r7-11 and right r16-20, points color8 (9,4),(10,4),(11,3); fills color8 paths: row9/10 c1-3 then 4 terminal, row11 c1-2 then 4; bottom rows18-20 fill c0-4 color8; 
6) 29x12 bg6, color9 top-right c11 rows0-9 and left rows16-25; color0 points (16,6),(17,3),(19,2),(20,2),(21,7),(23,4),(25,9). Output rows0,1,3-5,7,9 fill 0 across c0-10, row16-25 generate rays from left marker toward each point, 4 at target; row18/22/24/26? details in transcript. 
7) 29x21 bg7, color3 right col20 rows15-18 and left col0 rows25-28; color9 points (15,7),(16,13),(18,15). Output point rows extend horizontal color9 from each point rightward to boundary 3, 4 immediately before 9 runs; left marker rows25-28 sends 9 across row25,26,28 but not row27.
8) 24x28 bg5, color6 top c0-6 and bottom row23 c18-24, color2 dot (6,22). Output draws vertical color2 c4 rows1-23, and preserves original dot as 4 (r6,c22), while vertical continues from dot to bottom. 
Core likely rule: each pair of perpendicular/opposite edge bars of a color define directional fills of background; isolated marker pixels of a distinct color produce rays oriented toward specific boundary based on edge-bar geometry, and 4 indicates terminus of drawn ray. Need use precise demo-derived rule rather than guesses. Previous submissions were all incorrect. One malformed final grid: row lengths wrong. Always validate every output row has same dimension before submitting.
